not a global optimum or a bath-aware controllability no-go.

## Bounded Readout-Weight And Terminal-Sector Tests

The ideal eigenvalue weights need not remain optimal after the bath deforms the
seven population effects. This possible source of failure was isolated by a
bounded convex variable-projection solve. For the certified 300 fs target-0
pulse, optimized single-exciton weights reduce the relative operator residual
only to `0.9282005056807507` and require `15.466608141391703` times the ideal
coefficient norm. Both locked gates fail.

The test was enlarged through four nested terminal-population families:

| Terminal family | Relative operator residual | Coefficient amplification |
|---|---:|---:|
| Seven single-exciton populations | `0.9282005056807507` | `15.466608141391703` |
| Ground plus seven single populations | `0.9178697130416876` | `17.82601713774511` |
| Ground, seven single, aggregate double | `0.9221034951951511` | `17.34327557758852` |
| All 29 resolved populations | `0.8506376230786722` | `32.06740893297959` |

All convex solves replay, but none crosses the `0.1` operator gate or the
`10`-fold coefficient-amplification gate. Even the uncalibrated pair-resolved
diagnostic therefore fails for this fixed pulse. This rules out a simple
detector-weight or terminal-sector repair of the 300 fs waveform, not another
pulse or detector family.

Ground, single, and double terminal populations are not third-order GSB, SE,
and ESA Liouville pathways. Those require ordered dipole interactions,
coherences, phase matching, and heterodyne detection. The terminal-sector result
must not be promoted as a finite-pulse spectroscopy theorem.

## Finite-Probe Heterodyne Result

A separate calculation now supplies the correctly typed endpoint spectroscopy
map. It propagates a finite probe from the HEOM population block to the retained
optical-coherence block, integrates a heterodyne detector row, and pulls that
functional back to a Hermitian `7 x 7` root effect by a backward adjoint solve.
SE and signed ESA are retained separately. GSB is not present because this
calculation deliberately restricts its input to the single-exciton root.

The locked molecular-frame `D1,K0` family contains 162 effects: three carrier
frequencies, three probe axes, three detector axes, and two heterodyne
quadratures. The independent gate verifies:

- full rank 49 on the real Hermitian root algebra;
- all four canonical targets in the unconstrained numerical span, with residual
  below `6.4e-14`;
- SE-plus-signed-ESA partition residual `1.734723475976807e-18`;
- direct-forward/backward-adjoint relative replay error
  `3.015373936610652e-08`.

The same certificate identifies the obstruction. The normalized effect matrix
has condition number `4011.379711876829`; the four minimum-norm exact
combinations require `L2` norms `97.18`, `79.76`, `147.84`, and `156.97`.
Under the locked `L2 <= 10` budget, the optimal target residuals are `0.7279`,
`0.5937`, `0.7332`, and `0.7958`. Thus the molecular-frame root-effect family is
algebraically complete at this rung, but a bounded calibrated readout from this
specific family is rejected.

The predeclared all-seven-carrier extension is also complete. It retains full
rank and improves the condition number from about `4011` to `936`. With the same
`L2 <= 10` and residual-at-most-`0.1` contract, targets 0, 1, and 2 now pass at
`0.0731581`, `0.0821238`, and `0.0867161`; target 3 remains open at
`0.3830062`. This is the certified three-of-four baseline from which the
predeclared temporal screen starts. Since both quadratures are retained, adding
phase-rotated copies cannot add a new real span.

The temporal screen has now executed. Two independently valid profiles pass
target 3 without cross-profile pooling. The selected `broad_probe_100fs` profile
has rank 49, condition number `410.33559810771516`, and passes all four bounded
targets with coefficient norms `6.2903`, `5.7355`, `7.2849`, and `8.4974` and
residuals near `1e-14`. The delayed-detector profile also passes target 3 at
`0.04378195`. The early profile is explicitly rejected because its adjoint-
forward replay error `5.2077e-8` exceeds the locked `5e-8` integrity threshold;
its smaller unchecked residual is not selected. Thus bounded four-target
readout is closed at the exploratory molecular-frame `D1,K0` tier.

## Next Constructive Exit

The predeclared normalized 300 fs direct-control screen returned relative operator
residual `0.997588` and is rejected at its locked `0.1` gate. Its exit clause
forbids the 24-segment and depth refinements for that control family, without
claiming a controllability no-go. The finite-probe route has crossed the bounded
gate and its selected broad profile is now executing at `D2,K0` and `D1,K1` under
the predeclared finite-convergence theorem. Only a stable result should advance
to GSB input completion and isotropic contraction. Physical `K_ij`, absolute
fields, disorder, orientation, covariance, and detector calibration remain later
gates.

